Unknown vs Not Observable vs Not Supported Logic

Implement strict logic.

Unknown

The scanner attempted to determine the value, but could not reach a reliable conclusion.

Examples:

Timeout
DNS failure
Partial handshake
CDN interference
Network interruption
Not Observable

The property cannot be determined from an external Internet-facing scan.

Examples:

Internal HSM
Source code cryptography
Database encryption
Internal PKI
Enterprise governance
Cryptographic inventory
Secrets management
Not Supported

The control was expected but is absent.

Examples:

Missing HSTS
Missing CAA
Missing OCSP
Missing SCT
Not Applicable

The control is irrelevant for the scanned service.

